<content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    Here are the first two terms of some different arithmetic sequences. What is the 5th term of each sequence?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item>–2, 4 ...
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 22</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>11, 111 ...
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 411</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item>5, 7.5 ...
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 15</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item>5, –4 ...
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>–31</para>
<br/>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    For each sequence, decide whether it could be arithmetic, geometric, or neither.
  </item><br/>
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      200, 40, 8, . . .
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> geometric</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      2, 4, 16, . . .
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> neither</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      10, 20, 30, . . .
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> arithmetic</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      100, 20, 4, . . .
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> geometric</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      6, 12, 18, . . .
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>arithmetic</para>
<br/>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    For each arithmetic sequence with missing terms, find the common difference that might help determine the missing terms.  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item>–3, –2, ___, ___, 1
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> 1; The missing terms are 1, 0.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      ___, 13, 25, ___, ___
     
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 12; The sequence should be 1, 13, 25, 37, 49.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      1, 0.25, ___, –1.25, ___
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>–0.75; The sequence is 1, 0.25, –0.5, –1.25, –2.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      92, ___, ___ ,___, 80
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>–3; The sequence is 92, 89, 86, 83, 80.</para>
<br/>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    Find the common difference for each of the following arithmetic sequences. <br/>
    HINT: It may be helpful to complete the sequence with the missing terms.    
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      ___, 6, 10, ___, 18
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 4; The sequence is 2, 6, 10, 14, 18.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>–1, ___, –11, –16, ___
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>–5; The sequence is –1, –6, –11, –16, –21.

</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      10, 5, ___, ___, –10
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> –5; The sequence is 10, 5, 0, –5, –10.

</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      ___, ___, 4.5, 6, ___
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>1.5; The sequence is 1.5, 3, 4.5, 6.

</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      ___, 12, 6, 0, ___
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> –6; The sequence is 18, 12, 6, 0, –6.</para></section>
</content>
